{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfhNtMSxrvDDbwjbN4XsP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The race is fixed: only the most recent search can now update results, loading, or errors, and clearing the query stays cleared even if an earlier request finishes afterwards.\n\n**Cause:** in `src/search/controller.ts`, every `search()` call wrote its outcome into state when its request settled, regardless of whether a newer search had started since.\n\n**Change** (`src/search/controller.ts` only, 6 lines added, 3 removed):\n- Each `search()` call takes a new request number from a counter, and its results, error, and loading updates are applied only if that number is still the latest.\n- Clearing the query also bumps the counter, so in-flight requests become stale; the clear itself was already synchronous and resets results, error, and loading immediately.\n- The public API is untouched, and so are the API adapter and the view.\n\n**Verification:**\n- The existing suite (`npm test`) passes, 4 of 4.\n- I also ran a temporary race check outside the repo using manually resolved promises, then deleted it; all three scenarios passed:\n  - a stale success is ignored and loading stays on;\n  - a stale error is ignored;\n  - a response arriving after a clear does not repopulate results.\n- No tests were modified and nothing was installed. The change is uncommitted in the working tree.\n\nSuperseded requests are ignored rather than aborted, so they still run to completion on the network. Cancelling them would mean adding an abort signal to `SearchApi.search`, which I left out to keep the API unchanged."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1702,"cache_read_input_tokens":10282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1702},"output_tokens":480,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"02d593b0-92da-40b9-bc32-7a650936213a","uuid":"da2d7eb7-5568-4ba0-9cd6-f075291e5162","timestamp":"2026-10-04T14:46:16.656Z","request_id":"req_011CfhNtM4dhu7go2tkpzAha"}
